Wait — actually is it a "no-op"? The re-entered `close()` cancels the timer (already null), sets `_server = null` (already null), and `if (server != null)` is false, so returns immediately. Yes, effectively a no-op with respect to awaiting the in-flight close. The comment is accurate.

